Commentary of al-Shinqiti (Adwa' al-Bayan) on surah 52, verse 46:

His saying, may He be exalted: ﴿On the Day when their scheming will avail them nothing whatsoever﴾.

In this verse, He—majestic and exalted—has made clear that the scheming of the disbelievers will avail them nothing in the Hereafter. This is in other than this place, as in His saying, exalted is He: ﴿This is the Day of Judgment; We have gathered you and the former peoples﴾ ﴿So if you have any scheme, then scheme against Me﴾ [al-Mursalat: 38-39].

He has also made clear that it does not benefit them in this world either:

• As in His saying, exalted is He, in this noble surah: ﴿Or do they intend a scheme? But those who disbelieve, they are the ones who will be ensnared by it﴾ [al-Tur: 42];

• And His saying: ﴿Indeed, they are scheming a scheme﴾ ﴿And I am scheming a scheme﴾, and the verse [al-Tariq: 15-16];

• And His saying: ﴿We will lead them step by step from where they do not know﴾ ﴿And I give them respite; indeed, My plan is firm﴾ [al-A'raf: 182-183];

and other verses besides these.
